2. Use anti-virus and anti-malware tools: Install reputable anti-virus and anti-malware programs on all devices that receive incoming emails so they can detect any malicious attachments before they reach your inbox.

3. Review your spam folder regularly: Regularly review your spam folder to look out for new messages with unknown sources or attachments that could contain malware.

4. Be cautious when clicking links in emails: Avoid clicking on links in emails unless you know who sent them and why they might have included malware.

5. Update your operating system and browser: Make sure both your operating system and web browsers are up-to-date to protect against known threats like phishing scams and malware attacks. 

